# Desktop build of the wgrender simple example.
#
# Run `./build.py desktop`: it builds wgrender's desktop library, writes
# build/desktop.hxml (where wgrender is on this machine, and how to link it) and
# then calls haxe with this file. Once that has run, plain `haxe build.hxml` works
# too — it just won't rebuild wgrender.
build/desktop.hxml

-cp src
--main Simple
--cpp build/cpp/desktop

# hxcpp names the binary after this (default: the main class).
-D HAXE_OUTPUT_FILE=simple

-dce full
-D analyzer-optimize
